# Copy to .env.local (gitignored). This file stays on this computer and covers
# local development plus common application settings.
#
# In development the Node API reads this file at startup. Restart `npm run dev`
# after changing runtime settings (proxy, search/fetch budgets, limits); ports,
# the database location and other startup values are read at startup only.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm run dev (local only: no SSH or WSL needed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API writes SQLite and uploaded files to ~/.matrius by default; set DATA_DIR
# below to store them elsewhere. The client's own IndexedDB stays inside the
# browser. Restart `npm run dev` after changing DATA_DIR.
# DEV_WEB_PORT=8081
# DEV_API_PORT=8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data root. Defaults to ~/.matrius (matrius.db and files/ live inside it).
# DATA_DIR=~/.matrius

# Application storage limit for uploaded files. Defaults to 128 MiB
# (128 * 1024 * 1024 bytes). This is a logical quota: the storage screen and
# upload checks use it instead of the host's free disk space.
# STORAGE_LIMIT_BYTES=134217728

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Common application settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Login session lifetime.
# AUTH_COOKIE_SECONDS=34560000
# Optional upstream proxy shared by web search and page fetching.
# When set, every web request uses it; there is no direct-connection fallback.
# WEBTOOL_PROXY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7890
